    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0747" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.5181/20: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-02T12:00:00+01:00">March 2,
                            1943—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>480. I raised this matter with the Foreign Minister on February 22 along the
                    lines of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> transmitted with my
                    despatch number 573 of January 15.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d786-f1"/> Jordana said
                    that after all Spain does <pb facs="0748" n="736" xml:id="pg736"/> recognize the
                    Vichy Government which had the right to get rid of Consuls disloyal to it.
                    Without withdrawing from the position taken in my <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi>, I pointed out that this was a practical matter and
                    expressed the hope that the Government would discourage the supplanting of the
                    present French Consuls and any disturbance to the <hi rendition="#italic">status
                        quo</hi>. Jordana said he would give consideration to my views but gave no
                    assurances.</p>
                <p>Your 456, February 27, midnight.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d786-f2"/> Repeated to
                    Tangier and Algiers for R. Murphy.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d786-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d786-f1" n="31" xml:id="d786-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; see telegram No. 101, January 14, midnight, <ref target="#pg733"
                        >p. 733</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d786-f2" n="32" xml:id="d786-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 29, <ref target="#pg735">p. 735</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d786-f3" n="33" xml:id="d786-f3-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, Special Representative of the President in French North Africa
                    and U.S. Political Adviser on the Staff of the Supreme Commander, Allied
                    Expeditionary Force in North Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
